WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.340
Speaker 1: I was assuming we would start today's&nbsp;
show by talking about the new Republican speaker&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:09.660
of the House of Representatives, because, after&nbsp;
all, Republicans took over, even though it was by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:14.580
a small margin, the control of the House based on&nbsp;
their wins in the 2022 midterm election November&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:19.860
8th. And it was time yesterday for them to&nbsp;
select a new speaker of the House. But no,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:25.860
they have not done it. And Republicans are in the&nbsp;
midst of what is one of the biggest humiliating,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:32.580
self-inflicted embarrassments in recent American&nbsp;
political history. Republicans have suffered a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:39.180
true humiliation, failing to elect a speaker of&nbsp;
the House after three rounds of voting. The House&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:44.280
ultimately adjourning yesterday without speaker,&nbsp;
and they will start again today and they're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:51.480
likely already going right now as you listen to&nbsp;
today's program. Most Republicans voting for Kevin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:57.720
McCarthy, but not all. There is a faction that&nbsp;
has opted not to support Kevin McCarthy and this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:04.080
actually led to Hakeem Jeffries on the Democratic&nbsp;
side, with Democrats united behind Jeffries&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:11.040
actually coming closer to the 218 votes that are&nbsp;
needed than McCarthy in some of the votes. CNBC&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:16.260
has a good, nice, concise article about it by&nbsp;
Christina Wilkie. The House of Representatives&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:21.660
adjourned for the day Tuesday without a speaker&nbsp;
after Republican leader Kevin McCarthy failed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:28.140
three consecutive votes to secure enough support&nbsp;
to be selected to the post. This is a historic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:34.140
situation. It's an historic situation. Some are&nbsp;
even saying it's the first time in 100 years&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:42.300
that the majority party failed to coalesce around&nbsp;
a candidate to speaker in this number of votes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:46.200
And we don't know what the step is. The next step&nbsp;
is at this point in time. We will get to that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:52.500
After the first ballot resulted in votes for&nbsp;
several Republicans. The next two rounds saw&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:57.660
McCarthy's opponents coalesce around a new&nbsp;
contender, Congressman Jim Jordan of Ohio,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.660 --> 00:02:05.400
a longtime McCarthy ally. Jim Jordan says he&nbsp;
doesn't want it. And Lauren, Bob Baer and Scott&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:10.500
Perry are saying Jim Jordan is sort of like George&nbsp;
Washington. George Washington didn't want to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:16.260
president, but he did it. And they are talking&nbsp;
about Jim Jordan in the same delusional terms,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:23.460
which we will get to a little bit later. What&nbsp;
does this mean for the long term of the Republican&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:28.920
Party's ability to. I was going to say govern.&nbsp;
But it's like they don't really plan to govern the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:34.500
government. They plan to investigate Hunter Biden,&nbsp;
which we will also get to a little bit later. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:39.900
this is embarrassing. And Tucker Carlson is&nbsp;
saying it's becoming a joke. Sean HANNITY is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:45.960
saying that it is becoming a joke and we don't&nbsp;
exactly know the direction this will ultimately&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:55.320
go. The CNBC article also pointed out during each&nbsp;
of the three voice votes, every Democrat rallied&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.320 --> 00:03:00.240
unanimously around incoming minority leader&nbsp;
Hakeem Jeffries, a former guest on this program,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:06.540
by the way. But a sect of conservative Republicans&nbsp;
split from their party to back other candidates,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:12.420
including Jim Jordan, as I mentioned, in an&nbsp;
unexpected twist. McCarthy lost support as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:18.240
the voting continued, which is just hilarious to&nbsp;
see when in the third round, Florida Republican&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:25.500
Congressman Byron Donalds announced his support&nbsp;
for Jordan after voting twice for McCarthy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:33.540
as a result of Donald's defection, McCarthy got&nbsp;
202 of the 218 votes needed. Jeffries got to 12,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:43.260
getting quite close, in fact. Now, is it likely&nbsp;
that Hakeem Jeffries is going to be the speaker&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:49.620
of the House of Representatives? It is not likely.&nbsp;
And there are headlines saying, could Democrats&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:57.840
end up with the speakership? I don't believe that&nbsp;
it is likely. I believe a more likely scenario is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:06.240
if Republicans don't move to someone else, that&nbsp;
some Democrats end up joining the majority of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:11.280
Republicans. But AOC is saying that's not going&nbsp;
to happen and that Democrats are going to remain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:16.260
united. So I think the least likely scenario is&nbsp;
Hakeem Jeffries becomes the speaker of the House,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.260 --> 00:04:23.400
but it's not a zero chance. And man, that would be&nbsp;
unbelievable. So that's what happened yesterday. I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:29.400
have no news for you about the next speaker of the&nbsp;
House. Maybe we will later today. But of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:33.720
everyone on the Republican side weighing&nbsp;
in about this. One of those people,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:38.880
the failed former president Donald Trump. Let's&nbsp;
talk about that because it's quite interesting.

